Subject: notifier: label the "Restart is required" actions "Restart" and "Shut Down"

The notification is shown when a backend reports needsReboot, after its
updates are installed and wait only for the restart. Its two actions
open the logout prompt's reboot and shut-down pages (promptReboot,
promptShutDown) and start no update, so "Update and Restart" and
"Update and Shut Down" offer an update that is already done. Label
them for what they do.

--- a/notifier/DiscoverNotifier.cpp
+++ b/notifier/DiscoverNotifier.cpp
@@ -424,8 +424,8 @@ void DiscoverNotifier::showRebootNotification()
     notification->setText(i18n("The system needs to be restarted for the updates to take effect."));
     notification->setIconName(QStringLiteral("system-software-update"));
 
-    auto restartAction = notification->addAction(i18nc("@action:button", "Update and Restart"));
-    auto shutdownAction = notification->addAction(i18nc("@action:button", "Update and Shut Down"));
+    auto restartAction = notification->addAction(i18nc("@action:button", "Restart"));
+    auto shutdownAction = notification->addAction(i18nc("@action:button", "Shut Down"));
     connect(restartAction, &KNotificationAction::activated, this, &DiscoverNotifier::rebootPrompt);
     connect(shutdownAction, &KNotificationAction::activated, this, &DiscoverNotifier::shutdownPrompt);
 
